# WoW: Forever ONLY (Josh 2026-09-18). One client, one interface number, no
# compatibility shims: nothing here has to run on Era, Mists or retail, and
# the code is free to assume this game's rules - two-part names above all.
## Interface: 16001
## Title: BeebMod
## Notes: Small utilities for WoW: Forever, set from one window and one button.
## Author: Josh
## Version: 0.1.0-beta.10
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1711982
# TWO VARIABLES, NOT ONE (Josh 2026-09-20). BeebModDB is the whole book -
# every character ever seen, a megabyte and a half of it. BeebModKeep is
# only what you WROTE: the notes, the tags, the ratings, the settings. A few
# kilobytes.
#
# They are separated because losing the book is an inconvenience and losing
# your notes is not, and because this client hands back neither reliably: if
# the small one returns and the big one does not, the cause is size, and we
# will know that the first time it happens.
## SavedVariables: BeebModDB, BeebModKeep
# And a THIRD, per character rather than per account. It holds the same few
# kilobytes as the second one, and it exists to answer a question no amount of
# reading the file can: the client writes account saved variables correctly and
# hands back nothing, and per-character ones are a different file written by
# different code. If this one comes back when the others do not, everything
# moves here and the problem is over.
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: BeebModChar

# THE CLIENT READS SAVED VARIABLES AGAIN (Josh 2026-09-24). Build 70009
# hands an addon its saved variables back (checked with a probe addon: a
# fresh launch and a /reload both returned the table), so the book loads the
# ordinary way. The Data\Live link that ran the last save as addon code while
# the client could not - the ForeverSVFix trick - is retired, and so is the
# line that loaded it: anyone else installing the addon has no such link.
